An X11 window's minimized state (Task 33 of docs/plans/20261014-gpui-frontend.md): GPUI reads an X11 window's
`_NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN`, which a window manager sets on an iconified window, but keeps it to itself, and `window.list`
reports `minimized` from it as the GTK build reads GDK's minimized state there. The X11 client notes the state each
time it reads the window's `_NET_WM_STATE` and forgets the window when it goes; `gpui_linux::x11_window_minimized`
reads it by the window's X id. Additive; Wayland (whose xdg-shell has no minimized state) and the other platforms are
unchanged. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

